From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 15:51:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 22/26] mysql: make pooled connections cancellation-safe

Own each direct MySQL operation, streamed collection, and lease transaction through a cancel-on-drop guard. Preserve a pooled connection only after the protocol response is complete, poison transaction ownership after interrupted methods, and install replacements only after the failed transport has been removed and force-closed.

Vendor the pinned mysql_async revision and add a synchronous force-disconnect path that bypasses result draining and COM_QUIT while releasing pool accounting. Wake a recycler blocked in concurrent shutdown when direct discard removes the final in-use connection.

Default to client-side force-disconnect without numeric server cancellation. Add an explicit trusted-single-namespace topology assertion for an optional serial control lane that keeps the target transport alive through KILL CONNECTION, rejects stale physical generations, uses separately bounded control capacity, and fails closed after control replacement or failure.

Export bounded cancellation request, terminal-outcome, and latency metrics. Document the ownership contract, topology hazard, vendored-driver delta, strict activation setting, build-context inclusion, and focused verification requirements.
